include/ikd-Tree/{ikd_Tree.h,ikd_Tree.cpp} -- the vendored ikd-tree.

One patch per upstream file; the declaration and its definition are one
change and neither compiles without the other, so both files are here.

The pinned RESPLE ikd-tree is the same lineage/version as DALI-SLAM's. Its
background subtree rebuild may otherwise begin between measurement batches
and make correspondence searches depend on scheduler timing. Expose a
quiescence barrier (called from processData, see 01-resple-node.patch) and
initialize pthread_t so the existing conditional join is defined if thread
creation fails.

The barrier also covers a rebuild queued in Rebuild_Ptr before the background
worker acquires rebuild_ptr_mutex_lock. The estimator thread is the only
rebuild scheduler at this boundary, so no new job can be queued while it waits.

Scope: this makes the tree quiescent for the estimator's own correspondence
searches, which is where a mid-rebuild search would change the result (tree
*contents* stay consistent regardless -- Rebuild_Logger replays operations
that land during a rebuild). It does not cover Add_Points' internal
downsample searches, which can run against a rebuild that Add_Points itself
triggered earlier in the same mapIncremental() call.

